      "message": "Loop Simplification: \n\nfor this config, I have noticed that `IMAGE_HEIGHT \u003d ELAN_DMA_LOOP`. Is this the case for all sensors using `elan_image_read_linewise`. If so, I believe you can simplify the for loop:\n\nThe inner loop for (int y \u003d 0; y \u003c IMAGE_HEIGHT / ELAN_DMA_LOOP; y++) will only execute for y \u003d 0 because IMAGE_HEIGHT equals ELAN_DMA_LOOP. This loop can be removed, and y can be replaced by 0 in the index calculations within to improve clarity.\n\n```\n// Simplified index calculations after removing the \u0027y\u0027 loop\nrx_index \u003d x * 2;\nshort_raw[x + i * IMAGE_WIDTH] \u003d (rx_buf[rx_index] \u003c\u003c 8) + rx_buf[rx_index + 1];\n```",
